 us to open  presents and spend all day together on  face time and the last one is plot  connection and plot connection includes  any relevance to the plot but also the  characters in their stories so with  those three parameters in mind i've  analyzed five shows all the way through  every episode including ted lasso mythic  quest morning show trying and defending  jacob experts watching for product  placement use a handy guide for  determining where a product appears in  frame and so we usually split the screen  into nine quadrants nine little squares  inevitably viewers attentions are much  more on the middle quadrant and so a  brand that's actually more centered is  going to get a lot more attention than  the brand that's on the periphery  and you guessed it in my analysis apple  products appeared most often in section  5. those scenes typically started with  them on the periphery near section 7 8  and 9. based on my analysis ted lasso  had the most product sightings per  minute over 14 episodes apple gadgets  and services were spotted around 230  times  in the episode mentioned earlier nearly  half the sightings were in the center of  the screen not far behind was the  morning show over 10 episodes in its  first season apple products were spotted  around 250 times though the episodes are  twice as long in the episode with the  most sightings 12 of the 33 placements  were centered while mythic quest trying  and defending jacob didn't have nearly  as many integrations apple products and  services were frequently right in the  middle  audio placements are more subtle but can  be just as powerful  so the audio can be anything and in fact  if a sound like a jingle or logo or a  you know male kind of signal  is making people think about a brand  that also counted as a product placement  at the brand placement reference to the  brand in the consumer's mind and ted  lasso some of it's pretty obvious yeah  just a little note to myself tell me to  buy apple stock we are now sharing an  icloud account  and the characters of mythicquest and  trying love to  hello it's not working i'm gonna go  facetime my kids  no  no no  this is an audio facetime you see me now  and our last and most subtle of the  product placement dimensions plot  connection think of apple gadgets as  literal plot devices they're being used  to move stories forward and develop  characters take this example from ted  lasso when after much indecision ted  commits to signing his divorce papers  from beginning to end of this storyline  the iphone was involved acting as a  connective tissue between ted and his  soon-to-be ex-wife finally he even uses  the iphone camera to scan the contract  and send it back to the lawyer and then  there's this one scene in trying where  the leading characters jason and nikki  are gathered around a macbook to await  an update on their child adoption  process or in mythic quest during their  pandemic episode airpods are used not  only to connect nearly every character  but they're on screen for about 18  minutes of the 24 minute episode and of  course plot is attached to characters  most consumers when they watch a show  especially tv series where to develop  these sort of  life-like relationships which are called  parasocial relationships with the  characters they feel like they get to  know them and so if you see the  character associated with a product in a  in a tv series or in a story your  feelings and attitudes toward the  character are going to transfer over to  that brand my analysis showed that these  likable main characters are the ones  most frequently shown with apple  products in ted lasso over the course of  14 episodes rebecca welton a character  whose arc bends from antagonist to ted  lasso ally is most often seen with apple  products around 70 times while ted has  spotted nearly 60 times with various  apple products  jason and nikki the similarly likable  and funny leads in trying are seen in  every episode of season 2 with iphones  in the morning show the two leading  ladies bradley and alex lead the pack  with iphone sightings each was seen with  an iphone around 30 times in 10 episodes  according to previous reports apple  specifically limits villains and bad  guys from appearing with its products  apple declined to comment on those  reports but i found lots of evidence of  that myself  in mythic quest joe a power hungry and  manipulative main character who is at  one point described as conservative is  seen almost exclusively with an  unbranded macbook also in that airpod  episode her hair was conspicuously  covering her ears in almost every shot  in the morning show bradley's absentee  father when first introduced is shown  with an unbranded flip phone  and in defending jacob leonard patz one  of the main characters uses an android  and also as a pedophile charged with  murder  so how does this all affect you and me  the viewers if a product placement is  effective your attitude will be more  positive  after watching an episode than before so  we measure pre and we measure posts and  we compare that  but really the sort of the best is to  see like well are they gonna buy a pepsi  and that's really hard to do in the case  of apple you've probably already bought  the product now you just like this guy  so much you might buy it again
 

